        {
          "say": "Remember the order with Dad Sat Tired.",
          "write": "Dad Sat Tired"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Make the units match",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "If speed is in kilometres per hour, time must be in hours.",
          "write": "km/h → km and hours"
        },
        {
          "say": "Change minutes to hours by dividing by 60.",
          "write": "40 min = 40/60 h"
        },
        {
          "say": "Careful. 2 hours 30 minutes is 2.5 hours, not 2.3.",
          "write": "2 h 30 min = 2.5 h",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 230,
            "alt": "Half an hour is 0.5 of an hour",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 480,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "white",
                "color": "black"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 240,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "teal",
                "change": "highlight",
                "label": "30 min = 0.5 h"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 190,
                "text": "2.3 h",
                "size": 36,
                "color": "red",
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 430,
                "y": 190,
                "text": "2.5 h",
                "size": 36,
                "color": "green",
                "change": "add",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 130,
                "y": 190,
                "text": "1 hour →",
                "size": 22,
                "color": "black"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "A train goes 150 kilometres in 2.5 hours. Divide.",
          "write": "150 ÷ 2.5 = 60 km/h"
        },
        {
          "say": "Chloe cycles at 18 for 40 minutes. 18 times 40 over 60 is 12.",
          "write": "18 × 40/60 = 12 km"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Kilometres per hour and metres per second",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "One kilometre per hour is 1000 metres in 3600 seconds.",
          "write": "1 km/h = 1000 m / 3600 s"
        },
        {
          "say": "To change kilometres per hour to metres per second, divide by 3.6.",
          "write": "km/h ÷ 3.6 = m/s",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 230,
            "alt": "Divide by 3.6 one way, multiply the other",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 80,
                "w": 180,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "km/h"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 340,
                "y": 80,
                "w": 180,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "m/s"
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 225,
                "y": 105,
                "x2": 335,
                "y2": 105,
                "color": "purple",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 335,
                "y": 140,
                "x2": 225,
                "y2": 140,
                "color": "green",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 90,
                "text": "÷ 3.6",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "purple"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 190,
                "text": "× 3.6",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "So 72 kilometres per hour is 20 metres per second.",
          "write": "72 ÷ 3.6 = 20 m/s"
        },
        {
          "say": "Metres per second numbers are always the smaller ones.",
          "write": "m/s is smaller"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Average speed",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Max drives 60 kilometres at 40, then 60 kilometres at 60.",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y8/maths/speed-distance-and-time-two-part.svg",
          "alt": "Two equal 60 km parts at 40 and 60 km/h"
        },
        {
          "say": "First part takes 1.5 hours. Second part takes 1 hour.",
          "write": "1.5 h + 1 h = 2.5 h"
        },
        {
          "say": "Average speed is total distance over total time.",
          "write": "120 ÷ 2.5 = 48 km/h",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 230,
            "alt": "50 crossed out, 48 km/h is correct",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 80,
                "text": "(40 + 60) ÷ 2 = 50",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "red",
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 180,
                "text": "120 ÷ 2.5 = 48 km/h",
                "size": 34,
                "color": "green",
                "change": "add",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Not 50. He spent longer driving at the slower speed.",
          "write": "✗ 50 km/h"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "18 times 40 is 720 kilometres. Far too far for a bike!",
          "write": "✗ 18 × 40 = 720 km"
        },
        {
          "say": "Change minutes into hours first.",
          "write": "min ÷ 60 = h"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't average the speeds. Use total over total.",
          "write": "total ÷ total"
        },
        {
          "say": "Reality check. Walking is about 5, cycling about 20, highway about 100.",
          "write": "5, 20, 100 km/h"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "S equals D over T. D equals S times T. T equals D over S.",
          "write": "S = D÷T  D = S×T  T = D÷S",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 280,
            "alt": "D S T triangle",
            "items": [
